WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.100
Please welcome Noomi Rapace!

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.320
Spring just arrived!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.380
Do you like speed?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.120
I love speed.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.060
I'm a speed junkie.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.560
And I love cars, so yes, the two of us have that in common.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.440
You should join me in a race.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.060
Yes!

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.060
How exciting that would be!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:39.580
I would love to join!

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.600
You also want to join?

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.760
No!

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.880
I would watch.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.640
I would watch behind a protective wall.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.940
Do you drive yourself?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.420
I drive fast. I have a sports car ...

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.300
Which I love! I listen to really loud music.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.000
I think well when I'm in cars. Like you said ...

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.100
You can find your form of ventilation. I think that I've had speed as a ventilator.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.900
You are ...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.340
You're now working with scent. You're working on a perfume ...

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.420
... that you've helped develop.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.640
How much of a business woman are you?

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.100
I do things from the heart and from ...

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.120
... what I want to carry, what I want to share, what I want to give others.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.060
And that's what this perfume creation started with.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.300
It was something I needed desperately myself.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.640
And also something I wanted to give to others.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.660
The thing about scent, is that it is very much connected to our memory.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.180
Yes.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.420
What is your strongest memory of scent from your childhood?

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.240
It's incredible how much I remember ...

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.000
And how many memories from my childhood that are related to scent.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.940
Both sad and good memories.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.580
Boyfriends ...

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.120
Friends ...

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.800
And more than anything, my best friend, you could say, when I grew up ...

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.100
... who was a horse.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.560
An Icelandic horse with the name Eldur.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.700
And when I moved from home, I moved away when I was 15, I moved to Stockholm ...

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.940
And he was the one I missed, almost the most sometimes.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.880
It was his scent, the muzzle ...

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.960
I rarely cried when I was little, I hardly ever showed my emotions.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.840
So I would go out to the box, and he would come and lay his big muzzle on my shoulder.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.480
So I would feel the weight, and his breath ...

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.180
You know horses, they breathe ... They communicate via breathing.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.040
And I will never forget the smell of his muzzle.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.840
So I have a lot of strong memories of scent.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:45.320
What do you think is the worst, to smell too much sweat or too much perfume?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.980
Well, that's a nice question!

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.360
Well, some of us are a bit sensitive!

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.240
Absolutely.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.760
I think, rather not smell like sweat. But there's ...

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.080
... a lot of bad perfume, as well.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.600
Yeah, because it can be really bad if you wear too much.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.320
Oh God, yes, that's the worst thing!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.840
It can be quite aggressive, too.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.440
Like when you're a young man and a bit ...

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.880
... a little too generous.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.280
It feels like you're trying to hide something, then!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.020
What did the Rolling Stones smell like?

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.960
You did a video with them.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.140
It's actually incredible ...

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:34.020
Mick, who I know quite well, he has such a young spirit.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:39.420
And he danced non-stop for hours, and was sweating like ...

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.680
... really heavily, but he didn't smell at all!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.600
It was really ...

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.820
He feels like a really fresh person.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.120
But Keith Richards, he smells ..?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.180
I wasn't that close to Keith!

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.400
So I don't know if he smells.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.700
As I mentioned before, you broke your nose.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.600
In a scene with Orlando Bloom.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.560
An action scene.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.440
And since then, you haven't learned a thing, because you constantly injure yourself!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.460
You just did a film called Stockholm.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.240
Which is about the drama on Norrmalmstorg.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.680
And you got injured again?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:17.500
Yes.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.160
What happened this time?

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.800
I became blind!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.240
I got a chemical burn injury on both eyes.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.160
On one eye, I was blind for a week.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.080
And in the other, my sight returned in a couple of days. But it was probably the worst thing I ever experienced.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.020
In the end of the movie, about the drama on Norrmalmstorg ...

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:44.140
I think it was supposed to be the fifth day locked in a bank vault, and then the police sent in tear gas.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:52.220
And the agent that the make-up artists used to create tears, swollen eyes and redness ...

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.960
They had cut open a Vic nose spray.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.320
Which you're not supposed to use in your eyes.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.920
And they had just opened them, so I got ... From the alcohol itself ...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.540
A chemical burn injury.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.860
And I couldn't see anything.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.340
My friend and make-up artist, not the one who did this ...

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.460
... she had to help me go to the toilet, shower me, feed me ...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.300
I was completely invalid.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.340
But you've recovered now?

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.700
I'm perfectly fine now. But at the same time, it's a weird thing ...

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.580
... with actors, I laid there with my blindness and was thinking ...

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.600
«Now I know what it's like to be blind.»

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.240
«I can play blind now.»

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.920
It's like, you can use everything!

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.760
Noomi, you live in London. You've lived in London for quite some time.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:39.600
Yes.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:40.760
And ...

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.300
And, as I understand, you live with your sister?

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:44.040
Yes.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:44.680
Your little sister?

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:45.180
Yes.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.400
How old is she?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:47.340
23.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.840
Have you always been close?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.360
She is my best friend. She is my ...

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.640
I was like a mini mom for her, because she's 15 years younger than me.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.080
I moved from home when she was born, so we didn't spend our childhood together. But we're catching up!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:10.200
So I was like a mini mom for her, and then we became sisters, and then we became best friends. And now she's like a mini mom for me!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.300
She's like: «You have to sleep more!»

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:17.340
And if I've been out late at night, I will take off my heels and tip toe in ...

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.020
... and be completely quiet. And the next morning, she will ask me: «When did you go home?»

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.120
«2-ish?» «No, I heard you at 4!»

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.060
So we're very close. I love her and I'm incredibly grateful that she's in my life.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.800
When I see you again now, and it's been many years since we first met ...

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.020
You're different.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:40.980
In a way.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:41.760
How?

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.600
I might be wrong, but to me, you feel ...

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.780
... in some way, happier?

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:49.720
... than the first times we spoke together?

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.340
Yes?

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.960
Am I wrong or right?

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.680
No, but I feel happier.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:56.600
I feel ...

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.920
... like I've landed in myself.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.080
And that I ...

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:05.260
I can understand myself more. And that I have outlets for ...

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.780
... for everything that happens within me.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:12.420
I don't clinch that often, I have less conflicts.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.820
I'm less angry.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.980
I feel happier, and more calm.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.000
How did this happen?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.520
It's a hard question to answer.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.060
I think that I ... For people around me ... I grew up with ...

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:30.500
... a belief that you're strong when you're alone.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:36.840
And that you're not supposed to show weakness, you're not supposed to share, and you're not supposed to show when you're sad or ...

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.120
... insecure.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:45.220
But that means that you're completely in your own bubble. And it's hard to develop when you're alone.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.480
And I've learnt ...

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.580
... that it's not a weakness to know when to speak out about feeling insecure or sad or ...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.900
... or when you're in doubt.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.520
I feel like I'm wrong a lot of times. And I learn from people around me.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.660
And I just feel more open about that.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.080
If you were to choose ...

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.280
Today ...

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:11.740
... what you value the most ...

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:12.260
... of ...

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.060
... freedom or belonging?

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.100
Wow.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.440
What would you choose?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.060
Freedom, I think.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.660
Because within freedom, you can find belonging.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:33.920
But if I don't feel free, I'll break up any belonging.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.280
Good answer?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.760
Yes, a very good answer, I think.

